the headlines say that former president  trump was exonerated and violently  clearing out protesters for a photo op  at lafayette square last year those  headlines are wrong first of all this  report was incredibly narrow it looked  only to the actions of the u.s park  police it didn't look to the secret  service it didn't interview  attorney general william barr it didn't  talk about all of the bureau of prisons  officers who were in lafayette square  that day and second of all the facts  that are in this report are actually  incredibly damning if you actually read  the report  it does appear that the u.s park police  had a plan to clear protesters in order  to put up a fence  however the us park police had no idea  the president was going to be on site  until bill barr  came out informed them to which the park  police was incredulous  then minutes later before the park  police could even implement their plan  to give warnings to the protesters the  u.s secret service jumped the gun  and started violently attacking the  protesters on site and on top of that  the us park police were not authorized  to use cs gas and pepper balls which the  secret service  and the bureau of prisons employees were  actually using  there was much more to the story and  this is not an exoneration this still  appears to be exactly what it looks like
 

